    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'ve homed in on the user\'s core vision: a \"DIGITAL ZOOLOGY FIELD GUIDE / NATURAL HISTORY ATLAS.\" The aesthetic is now taking shape, drawing from forests, natural history museums, botanical field guides, old zoology textbooks, the Earth, and leaves. This visual identity is grounding my approach.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Palette**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the visual aspects. I envision a palette built from moss, wood, and parchment with natural textures and specimen collections as my base. It\'s an earthy mix of forest green, sage, warm beige, and terracotta tones, all set against a warm cream background with subtle paper grain and botanical silhouettes. For typography, I\'m thinking of a high-contrast editorial serif paired with a clean body serif or sans, with italicized scientific names. I\'m also ensuring the interface design is image-resilient, with fallback styles to maintain visual completeness.\n\n\n"
