    thinking: "**Defining Specimen Details**\n\nI\'m currently working on defining the specific identifications for each specimen in `src/data/nonChordata.ts`. I\'ve started with `hyalonema`, giving it the identification: \'Globular or rounded sponge body anchored into ocean silt by a long spirally twisted rope-like stalk of silicious spicules.\' I\'ll move on to `euplectella` next.\n\n\n**Adding Specimen Descriptions**\n\nI\'ve just added detailed descriptions for several more specimens. For `euplectella`, it\'s now: \'Curved cornucopia cylindrical sponge with an intricate geometric lattice of fused silicious spicules and an oscular sieve-plate.\' I also described `spongilla` as a \'Colonial, encrusting or branched freshwater sponge colored emerald green with abundant gemmules for overwintering.\' I\'ve also moved on to defining `physalia`, `millepora`, and other new specimens.\n\n\n**Adding Specimen Identifications**\n\nI\'ve just finished up the identifications. For `alcyonium`, it\'s \'Fleshy, leathery lobed colony without a hard axis, bearing star-like autozooids with eight pinnate tentacles.\' `gorgonia` is now \'Flat, planar, reticulate sea fan with interconnected branches supported by a flexible horny axial rod of gorgonin protein.\' `adamsia` is \'Solitary sea anemone with bilobed pedal disc wrapped around a hermit crab gastropod shell, armed with cinclides and acontia.\' Next, `pennatula` is \'Quill-like fleshy colony differentiated into a basal anchoring peduncle and an upper rachis with lateral polyp-bearing leaves.\' `fungia` is \'Large, solitary, unattached mushroom-shaped stony corallum with radiating skeletal septa resembling mushroom gills.\' Finally, `meandrina` is \'Massive hemispherical brain coral with sinuous meandering corallite valleys and steep collines resembling cerebral gyri.\'\n\n\n"
