          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      species: \'geniculata\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    accessionNo: \'INV-CNI-001\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    spotlightQuote: \'The quintessential polymorphic marine hydrozoan demonstrating clear alternation of polypoid and medusoid generations.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    shortDescription: \'Colonial, marine, trimorphic hydrozoan exhibiting alternation of generations between an asexual branching hydroid colony and free-swimming sexual medusae.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    identification: \'Delicate whitish-brown plant-like branched colony with bell-shaped hydrothecae and cylindrical gonothecae.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    habitat: \'Shallow coastal marine waters attached to brown kelp, rocks, pilings, and mollusk shells down to 80 meters.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    morphology: \'Arborescent colony rooted by a creeping horizontal stolon (hydrorhiza) producing upright branched stems (hydrocaulus). Colony exhibits polymorphism with three distinct zooids: gastrozooids (hydranths for feeding), blastostyles (gonozooids for asexual medusa budding), and free-swimming sexual medusae. The colony is shielded by a cuticular perisarc.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    anatomy: \'Living tissue is the coenosarc enclosing a continuous gastrovascular cavity. Gastrozooids are protected by a transparent wineglass-shaped cup (hydrotheca) and bear a circle of 24 filiform solid tentacles with nematocysts around an elevated hypostome mouth. Blastostyles are enclosed within cylindrical gonothecae.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    nutrition: \'Carnivorous filter-predator; gastrozooid tentacles capture micro-crustaceans and plankton using nematocysts, directing them into the hypostome for digestion in the continuous gastrovascular canal.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    reproduction: \'Classical metagenesis: the asexual sedentary polyp colony produces tiny saucers (medusa buds) on blastostyles by budding. Medusae escape, mature as dioecious sexual pelagic jellies, and release gametes into seawater. Fertilization produces a ciliated planula larva that settles to establish a new polyp colony.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    lifeCycle: \'Hydroid colony (asexual, diploid) \342\206\222 Medusa buds \342\206\222 Medusa (sexual, dioecious) \342\206\222 Egg & Sperm \342\206\222 Zygote \342\206\222 Ciliated Planula larva \342\206\222 Sessile Hydrula \342\206\222 Young Obelia colony.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    specialFeatures: \'Trimorphic colony (hydranths, blastostyles, medusae); the medusa possesses true marginal statocysts (lithocysts) for equilibrium and a reduced velum (velum is rudimentary or absent).\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    importance: \'Classic textbook organism demonstrating metagenesis (alternation of generations) and polymorphic specialization in metazoans.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    interestingFacts: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'The entire branching colony shares a single continuous \"stomach\" through which digested fluids pulse continuously.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Its free-swimming medusae are scarcely 1 to 2 mm in diameter when liberated.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Unlike Hydra, Obelia possesses an exoskeleton of amber-colored chitinous perisarc.\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    examPoints: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Class: Hydrozoa, characterized by craspedote/acraspedote medusa and acellular mesoglea.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Exhibits trimorphism: Hydranth (nutritive), Blastostyle (asexual budding), Medusa (sexual).\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Hydrotheca encloses hydranth; Gonotheca encloses blastostyle; perisarc covers hydrocaulus.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Medusa possesses 8 marginal statocysts (lithocysts) located at the bases of tentacles.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Larva is a solid, ciliated, free-swimming Planula.\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: \'physalia\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    commonName: \'Portuguese Man-of-War\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    scientificName: \'Physalia physalis\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    phylumId: \'cnidaria\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    classification: {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      kingdom: \'Animalia\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      phylum: \'Cnidaria\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      class: \'Hydrozoa\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      order: \'Siphonophorae\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      genus: \'Physalia\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      species: \'physalis\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    accessionNo: \'INV-CNI-002\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    spotlightQuote: \'A floating super-organism armada of specialized zooids capable of delivering agonizing neurotoxic stings.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    shortDescription: \'Free-floating colonial siphonophore featuring a large, iridescent blue-pink gas float (pneumatophore) and trailing tentacles with lethal nematocysts.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    identification: \'Iridescent blue-pink crested gas float (pneumatophore) supporting polymorphic colony with elongate dactylozooids.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    habitat: \'Tropical and subtropical warm pelagic waters of the Atlantic, Pacific, and Indian Oceans drifting with surface winds and currents.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    morphology: \'Consists not of a single organism, but a complex polymorphic colony of specialized zooids suspended from a crested, gas-filled bladder (pneumatophore) up to 30 cm long. Long trailing tentacles (dactylozooids) can extend 10 to 30 meters beneath the surface.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    anatomy: \'Extreme division of labor with four specialized polypoid and medusoid zooids: 1) Pneumatophore (modified medusoid float containing gas gland that secretes carbon monoxide and nitrogen); 2) Dactylozooids (defensive and prey-catching tentacular polyps packed with battering batteries of nematocysts); 3) Gastrozooids (feeding polyps with digestive enzymes); 4) Gonozooids (branched reproductive clusters).\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    nutrition: \'Predatory carnivore. Trailing dactylozooids paralyze fish, squid, and crustaceans with potent hypnotoxins; contracting tentacles lift prey upward to the cluster of open-mouthed gastrozooids, which spread over the fish and secrete proteolytic enzymes.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    reproduction: \'Gonozooids produce medusoids that generate gametes; external fertilization in open ocean waters produces pelagic larvae that develop into new floating colonies.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    specialFeatures: \'Pneumatophore contains up to 14% carbon monoxide produced by a specialized gas gland. Its nematocysts inject physaliatoxin\342\200\224a dangerous neurotoxic protein that can cause human cardiovascular collapse and severe dermal necrosis.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    importance: \'Medical hazard for marine swimmers; fascinating study in colonial polymorphic integration where individuals sacrifice autonomy for colony survival.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    interestingFacts: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'The float acts as a natural sailing rig: some colonies have floats aligned to the left (\"left-handed\") and others to the right, dispersing the species in opposite wind directions!\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Even dead, desiccated tentacles washed onto a beach can fire active nematocysts for weeks.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'The tiny shepherd fish (Nomeus gronovii) lives immune among the deadly tentacles, feeding on leftover food particles.\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    examPoints: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Class: Hydrozoa, Order: Siphonophorae.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Classic example of Polymorphism in animals with division of labor.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Four zooid types: Pneumatophore (float), Dactylozooid (defense/prey), Gastrozooid (nutrition), Gonozooid (reproduction).\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Float contains gas gland producing carbon monoxide (CO).\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Venom contains potent physaliatoxin causing extreme systemic pain and paralysis.\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: \'millepora\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    commonName: \'Fire Coral\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    scientificName: \'Millepora alcicornis\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    phylumId: \'cnidaria\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    classification: {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      kingdom: \'Animalia\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      phylum: \'Cnidaria\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      class: \'Hydrozoa\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      order: \'Anthoathecata\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      genus: \'Millepora\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      species: \'alcicornis\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    accessionNo: \'INV-CNI-003\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    spotlightQuote: \'A false coral of the hydrozoan lineage whose microscopic pores conceal searing, painful urticating cnidocytes.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    shortDescription: \'Colonial hydrocoral with a heavy calcium carbonate skeleton resembling true stony corals, infamous for painful burning stings on contact.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    identification: \'Encrusting or branching calcareous mustard-yellow hydrocoral skeleton perforated with cyclosystem pores.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    habitat: \'Shallow tropical coral reefs (1\342\200\22340 m) in warm Caribbean, Atlantic, and Indo-Pacific waters.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    morphology: \'Forms massive encrustations, leafy plates, or upright antler-like branching colonies with a mustard-yellow, tan, or greenish-brown hue. The skeleton surface appears smooth to the naked eye but is riddled with thousands of microscopic pin-prick pores.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    anatomy: \'A true hydrocoral (not an anthozoan). The skeleton (coenosteum) displays pores arranged in cyclosystems: a large central gastropore (containing a feeding gastrozooid) encircled by 5 to 7 smaller dactylopores (each housing a defensive, tentacle-like dactylozooid equipped with formidable nematocysts). Living tissue covers the skeleton in a thin surface layer.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    nutrition: \'Captures zooplankton through stinging dactylozooids that pass food to central gastrozooids; also relies on photosynthetic carbohydrates supplied by massive populations of endosymbiotic zooxanthellae.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    reproduction: \'Asexual growth via skeletal expansion and fragmentation; sexual reproduction by releasing tiny, short-lived medusoids from specialized ampullae in the skeleton.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    specialFeatures: \'Cyclosystem pore arrangement (one gastropore surrounded by dactylopores); extreme density of penetrating nematocysts causing intense burning dermatitis in divers.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    importance: \'Major structural contributor to shallow reef frameworks; significant biological hazard for recreational divers and snorkelers.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    interestingFacts: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Though called \"coral,\" it is closer kin to Hydra and Obelia than to true brain or staghorn corals.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'The burning sensation from contact can persist for days and leave pigmented scarring.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Encrusts dead gorgonian fans and shipwrecks at astonishingly rapid calcification rates.\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    examPoints: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Belongs to Class Hydrozoa (Hydrocorallina), NOT Class Anthozoa.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Forms a massive calcareous exoskeleton (coenosteum).\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Pores arranged in Cyclosystems: central gastropore surrounded by small dactylopores.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Zooids are dimorphic: Gastrozooids (feeding) and Dactylozooids (stinging/defense).\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Produces free-swimming, non-feeding medusoids from skeletal ampullae.\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    id: \'aurelia\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    commonName: \'Moon Jellyfish\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    scientificName: \'Aurelia aurita\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    phylumId: \'cnidaria\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    classification: {"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      kingdom: \'Animalia\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      phylum: \'Cnidaria\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      class: \'Scyphozoa\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      order: \'Semaeostomeae\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      genus: \'Aurelia\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      species: \'aurita\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    accessionNo: \'INV-CNI-004\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    spotlightQuote: \'A translucent saucer-shaped pelagic drifter displaying four violet horseshoe gonads and marginal sensory rhopalia.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    shortDescription: \'Free-swimming, saucer-shaped scyphomedusa with four distinctive horseshoe-shaped pinkish-violet gonads in its translucent bell.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    identification: \'Translucent saucer-shaped umbrella with four horseshoe-shaped gonads, four frilled oral arms, and eight marginal rhopalia.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    habitat: \'Coastal waters, estuaries, and sheltered bays worldwide, swimming near the surface in large aggregations.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    morphology: \'Bowl-shaped or saucer-shaped umbrella (subumbrella and exumbrella) measuring 20 to 40 cm in diameter, milky white and translucent. The umbrella margin is scalloped into eight marginal notches, each housing a sensory rhopalium flanked by two marginal lappets. The underside mouth is surrounded by four long, ruffled oral arms.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    anatomy: \'A true scyphomedusa lacking a velum (craspedote condition absent; acraspedote). Thick cellular mesoglea provides elasticity for swimming. Mouth leads into a central stomach giving off four gastric pouches, each bearing gastric filaments. A sophisticated gastrovascular system consists of 16 radial canals (branched perradial and interradial, unbranched adradial) opening into a circular ring canal at the margin.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    nutrition: \'Feeds on plankton, fish eggs, and flagellates. Swimming movements drive plankton onto the mucus-coated exumbrella; flagella beat particles toward the margin where oral arms scrape the food and convey it to the mouth for extracellular enzymatic digestion.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    reproduction: \'Dioecious with four horseshoe-shaped gonads in the gastric pouches. Fertilization occurs on the female\342\200\231s oral arms. Development yields a ciliated planula larva, which metamorphoses into a small polyp called the scyphistoma. The scyphistoma undergoes transverse fission (strobilation) into a pile of saucers, each maturing into a free-swimming eight-lobed ephyra larva.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    lifeCycle: \'Adult Medusa (male & female) \342\206\222 Planula larva \342\206\222 Sessile Scyphistoma (polyp) \342\206\222 Strobila (transverse budding) \342\206\222 Ephyra larva (juvenile medusa) \342\206\222 Adult Aurelia.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    specialFeatures: \'Eight sensory rhopalia containing a statocyst (lithocyst) for equilibrium and a pigment-cup ocellus for photoreception. Gastrovascular canal branching pattern with ring canal.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    importance: \'Classic laboratory specimen for teaching true jellyfish anatomy; key trophic link in pelagic coastal marine ecosystems.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    interestingFacts: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Its sting is so mild that human skin on the palms cannot feel it, though it can irritate sensitive eyelids or cuts.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Can tolerate extremely low dissolved oxygen levels that kill competing commercial fishes.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'In laboratory microgravity tests aboard the Space Shuttle, Aurelia jellyfish developed normally but struggled to orient when returned to Earth gravity.\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ],"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    examPoints: ["
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Class: Scyphozoa (true jellyfish), acraspedote (velum is absent).\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Eight marginal notches with Rhopalia (each with statocyst and ocellus).\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Four horseshoe-shaped gonads located in gastric pouches.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Strobilation: asexual transverse fission of scyphistoma into ephyra larvae.\',"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "      \'Gastrovascular system: 4 perradial, 4 interradial (branched), 8 adradial (unbranched), and 1 circular ring canal.\'"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "    ]"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
        lines {
          text: "  },"
          type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_UNCHANGED
        }
